course: dictionary
lesson: 7091
title: Pea
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pea is a small round green seed that grows inside a pod, and people eat it as a vegetable. The pea plant is a climbing plant that makes these pods. The context shows this: «Some seeds float on water, like coconuts, and some are shot out when the pod bursts open, like peas and some beans.» The pod is the case around the seeds, and the peas are the seeds inside it.
explain: Pea is a noun, so it names a thing, and its plural is peas. In «Ice or frozen peas should be wrapped in a cloth», the peas are something you can hold and use, like other vegetables. As food, peas give you fibre and protein.
explain: Words can also work in phrases. «Like two peas in a pod» means very alike, not that two peas are really in a pod. «Pea-sized hail» means hail as small as a pea. For phrases, think about the whole group of words, not each word on its own.
fact: A pea is a small round green seed that grows in a pod.
fact: «The bee hummingbird from Cuba is the smallest bird in the world; it weighs about two grams and lays eggs the size of a pea.»
fact: The pea plant is a climbing plant, and it grows pods.
fact: «Ice or frozen peas should be wrapped in a cloth and used for about 15 to 20 minutes at a time, because ice on bare skin can burn.»
fact: Whole peas can choke very young children, so keep them away from little ones who might swallow them whole.
exercise: «The bee hummingbird lays eggs the size of a pea.» What does this tell you about the eggs? | *The eggs are very small and round | The eggs are as big as a house | The eggs are green and taste sweet
exercise: In «Some seeds ... are shot out when the pod bursts open, like peas», what is a pod? | A kind of bird | A climbing plant with leaves | *The case that grows around the seeds | A green vegetable soup
exercise: Jess says «like two peas in a pod» means two peas are sitting in a pod. What does the phrase really mean? | Very hungry | Very far apart | *Very alike | Two small green seeds in a box
test: In «Eat your peas or you won't get pudding», which word sounds stricter? | *or | and | pudding | peas
test: What is a pea plant? | A tree with pink flowers | *A climbing plant that grows these pods | A bird that lays eggs | A brown nut from a shop
exam: Which is the best meaning of pea? | A small bird that lays eggs | *A small round green seed that grows in a pod and is eaten as a vegetable | A grain of sand from the beach | A large brown nut from a tree
